0.0.36ebd59484fb5a560bc8936f449c815daa9a9e55.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.36ebd59484fb5a560bc8936f449c815daa9a9e55.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued November 2 at 12:31PM MST until November 5 at 5:15PM MST by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding along the San Juan River caused by excessive\nrainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...along the San Juan River from the Four Corners through\nMexican Hat, UT. This includes Bluff, Montezuma Creek and Aneth.\n\n* WHEN...Until 515 PM MST Thursday.\n\n* IMPACTS...River levels continue to rise due to excess runoff from\nSunday's rainfall. Expect high water levels and the River exceeding\nits banks, inundating low-lying areas along the San Juan River. A\nprolonged period of high water is forecast, with a crest near 23.5\nft Thursday morning. It will take several hours for all the water\nfrom these storms to work through local drainage systems.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1222 PM MST, stream gauge reports upstream and impacts of\nflooding have been reported along the San Juan River near\nFarmington, NM. Expect flood waters to reach the Four Corners\nWednesday evening and the town of Bluff early Thursday morning.\nTiming of crest is subject to change as more details become\navailable. Please continue to monitor the forecast and updated\nwarnings.\n- At 11:30 AM MST Monday the stage was 20.4 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 22.0 feet.\n- Forecast...The river will rise to 22 feet late this evening with\na secondary crest near 23.5 feet expected near Bluff early\nThursday morning. It will then fall below flood stage Thursday\nmorning.\n- Flood stage is 23.0 feet.\n\n- Http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMexican Hat, Bluff, Montezuma Creek, and Aneth.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-11-05T17:15:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Montezuma, CO; San Juan, UT","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.00b8de8d3d582a70415755093091fe5b78bb2bcf.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.00b8de8d3d582a70415755093091fe5b78bb2bcf.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-11-03T05:33:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 030533 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 1033 PM MST Mon Nov 2 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Rivers across southwest CO and southeast UT remain high due to runoff. Several flood warnings will be in effect through Tuesday morning. - Tuesday will be dry with below normal temperatures. - A system is expected on Wednesday into Thursday morning. It wil","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-11-03T06:35:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... This is an automatically generated forecast with no discussion. The normal Fire Weather Forecast will resume in its entirety in the spring. ...GUSTY ERRATIC WINDS CAN BE EXPECTED NEAR ANY SHOWERS OR THUNDERSTORMS... ...THE SMOKE DATA IS CALCULATED FROM AN AVERAGE AT 6000 FEET MSL... COZ200-031100- Little Snake Forecast Area- 1135 PM MST Mon Nov 2 2026","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"mnc01","station_name":"Mancos","distance_km":5.1,"soil_temp_5cm_f":45.24,"soil_temp_15cm_f":48.54,"soil_moisture_5cm":null,"soil_moisture_15cm":null,"precip_in":null,"eto_in":null,"vapor_pressure":null,"solar_radiation":0.03,"wind_speed_mph":5.63,"air_temp_f":37.92,"relative_humidity":0.811,"url":"https://coagmet.colostate.edu/station/mnc01"},"aviation":{"icao":"KCEZ","distance_km":0,"raw_metar":"SPECI KCEZ 021537Z AUTO 29009KT 10SM BKN009 OVC015 06/05 A3001 RMK AO2 RAE17 CIG 007V011 P0000 T00610050","temp_f":43,"wind_dir":290,"wind_kt":9,"gust_kt":null,"visibility":"10+","cover":"OVC","flight_category":"IFR","altimeter":1016.3,"observed":1793633820,"raw_taf":null,"url":"https